<section class="sectionScience">
    <div class="sectionInner">
        <h2>The Science Behind the Technique</h2>
        <p class="sectionSubheading">Shadowing has decades of research behind it. It's one of the most studied pronunciation training methods in second language acquisition.</p>
        <div class="studyCards">
            <div class="studyCard">
                <div class="studyStat">30–40% better listening comprehension</div>
                <div class="studySource">Hamada, 2016, Language Teaching Research</div>
                <p>Shadowing training significantly improved phoneme perception and word recognition, with lower-proficiency learners showing the largest gains.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="studyCard">
                <div class="studyStat">25% more accurate pronunciation</div>
                <div class="studySource">Foote &amp; McDonough, 2017, Journal of Second Language Pronunciation</div>
                <p>Mobile-based shadowing produced significant gains in pronunciation accuracy and prosodic fluency (intonation and rhythm).</p>
            </div>
            <div class="studyCard">
                <div class="studyStat">82% reported less speaking anxiety</div>
                <div class="studySource">Trần Văn Hòa, 2020</div>
                <p>Consistent shadowing practice significantly reduced speaking anxiety and built confidence in students who previously avoided speaking opportunities.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
